/// \defgroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more More W3D draw modules: model, tank, truck, horde, sail, wake and stream
/// \ingroup grp_w3d_rendering
/// \brief Eight more of BFME 2's W3D draw modules, the factory functions
///        the module factory calls to build them and their module data,
///        and one truck helper, W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated.
///
/// This group continues \ref grp_w1021_w3d_draw_module_factories, which
/// explains what a draw module is, how W3DModuleFactory::init registers
/// each module name with an instance factory and a data factory, and when
/// the module factory calls the two (the data factory while INI loads, the
/// instance factory when a drawable is built). Read that page first; this
/// one covers what differs for the modules here.
///
/// \par What is documented here
/// - Instance factories (\c friend_newModuleInstance) of W3DScriptedModelDraw,
///   W3DHordeModelDraw, W3DTankDraw, W3DTruckDraw, W3DSailModelDraw,
///   W3DBoatWakeModelDraw and W3DProjectileStreamDraw.
/// - Data factories (\c friend_newModuleData) of W3DTankDraw, W3DTruckDraw,
///   W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData, W3DStreakDrawModuleData,
///   W3DSailModelDrawModuleData, W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData and
///   W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData. The instance factory of
///   W3DStreakDraw and the data factory that "W3DScriptedModelDraw" uses
///   (W3DModelDraw::friend_newModuleData) are not covered here.
/// - W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated, which keeps the truck module's
///   cached bone indices in step with its render object.
///
/// \par Registrations
/// Each pairing below was read from the body of W3DModuleFactory::init.
/// Every call registers the name as a draw module with the draw interface
/// mask, as for the modules on the w1021 page.
/// | Module name | Instance factory | Data factory | Extra function |
/// |---|---|---|---|
/// | W3DScriptedModelDraw | W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DModelDraw::friend_newModuleData | its own |
/// | W3DHordeModelDraw | W3DHordeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData | shared (see below) |
/// | W3DTruckDraw | W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleData | shared |
/// | W3DTankDraw | W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleData | shared |
/// | W3DStreakDraw | W3DStreakDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DStreakDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData | none |
/// | W3DSailModelDraw | W3DSailModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DSailModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData | none |
/// | W3DBoatWakeModelDraw | W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData | none |
/// | W3DProjectileStreamDraw | W3DProjectileStreamDraw::friend_newModuleInstance | W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData | none |
///
/// The last column is the further function that BFME 2's registration call
/// takes and Zero Hour's \c addModule does not. W3DHordeModelDraw,
/// W3DTruckDraw and W3DTankDraw pass the same one as W3DQuadrupedDraw and
/// W3DSupplyDraw; W3DScriptedModelDraw passes one used by no other draw
/// module. What these functions are for is not established here.
///
/// \par The model draw family
/// - **No module is registered as "W3DModelDraw".** Zero Hour registers
///   its general model draw module under that name. BFME 2's
///   W3DModuleFactory::init registers none; instead the name
///   "W3DScriptedModelDraw" gets W3DModelDraw's data factory, so a
///   W3DScriptedModelDraw block takes exactly the shared model draw fields
///   (the table W3DModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse registers). BFME 1's
///   W3DModuleFactory::init in Open-BFME-1 registers the same
///   "W3DScriptedModelDraw" name and also has no "W3DModelDraw".
/// - **One constructor under the family.** The constructors of
///   W3DHordeModelDraw, W3DSailModelDraw, W3DTankDraw and W3DTruckDraw (and
///   of W3DQuadrupedDraw and W3DSupplyDraw on the w1021 page) each run the
///   W3DScriptedModelDraw constructor first, and that constructor runs the
///   DrawModule constructor directly.
/// - **Shared fields.** The data of W3DHordeModelDraw, W3DSailModelDraw,
///   W3DTankDraw and W3DTruckDraw is built on W3DModelDraw's module data,
///   and each data class's \c buildFieldParse adds the shared model draw
///   table as well as its own, so those blocks accept every model draw
///   field plus the fields on their class pages. The tank, truck and sail
///   tables are added after the shared one; W3DHordeModelDraw adds its own
///   table first.
/// - W3DBoatWakeModelDraw and W3DProjectileStreamDraw are not model draw
///   modules: their constructors run the DrawModule constructor, and their
///   data has only its own fields.
///
/// \par Where the classes come from
/// - Zero Hour classes: W3DModelDraw, W3DTankDraw, W3DTruckDraw and
///   W3DProjectileStreamDraw. Zero Hour has no W3DScriptedModelDraw; its
///   tank and truck draw modules derive from W3DModelDraw.
/// - BFME 1 (Open-BFME-1's \c game/ tree and its W3DModuleFactory::init):
///   W3DScriptedModelDraw, W3DHordeModelDraw and W3DStreakDraw, plus the
///   tank and truck modules. BFME 1 does not register
///   W3DProjectileStreamDraw.
/// - In neither: W3DSailModelDraw and W3DBoatWakeModelDraw.
///
/// \par Modding
/// - Data-driven: which objects carry these modules (a
///   `Draw = <module name> ModuleTag_...` line in the \c Object block) and
///   the fields listed on each class page; the model-based modules also
///   take every shared model draw field.
/// - Hard-coded: the module names, which data factory each name uses (for
///   example that "W3DScriptedModelDraw" takes only the shared model draw
///   fields), and what each module does with its fields. A new kind of
///   draw module needs a new class and a new W3DModuleFactory::init
///   registration.
/// - Model draw data is not draw-only: the game logic reads it.
///   Weapon::calcProjectileLaunchPosition and
///   Object::getSingleLogicalBonePositionOnTurret call
///   Drawable::getProjectileLaunchOffset, which asks the drawable's draw
///   modules, and W3DScriptedModelDraw::getProjectileLaunchOffset answers
///   from the bone and barrel data of the best-matching condition state in
///   its module data (Zero Hour's Weapon::calcProjectileLaunchPosition uses
///   the same Drawable query). So the models, bones and condition states
///   set in W3DScriptedModelDraw blocks, and in the tank, truck, horde and
///   sail blocks that take the same model draw fields, change where
///   projectiles start, a simulation result that must be identical on every
///   machine in a multiplayer game.
/// - All draw module fields also sit in \c Object blocks, so they count
///   toward the INI data that multiplayer compares
///   (\ref sub_rts_model_modding).
///
/// \par Remastering
/// Some modules here advance their animation state by a fixed step per call
/// rather than per elapsed time: in BFME 2, W3DBoatWakeModelDraw's speed
/// ratio moves once per draw, and W3DSailModelDraw's damping limit applies
/// per call of the model draw transform adjustment, which runs at least once
/// per draw of the model and also on transform changes and polygon or ramp
/// queries (see their class pages); in Zero Hour, W3DTankDraw's tread
/// scroll moves once per draw. A renderer that draws at a different rate
/// changes how fast these animate.
///
/// \see W3DModuleFactory::init, ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI,
///      ModuleFactory::newModule, INI::initFromINIMultiProc,
///      \ref grp_w1021_w3d_draw_module_factories, \ref sub_w3d_rendering,
///      \ref sub_objects_modules


/// \class W3DModelDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief The general model draw code: shows an object's W3D model for its
///        current model condition, with animations, bones, particle effects,
///        shadows and decals.
///
/// Zero Hour: W3DModelDraw is the main draw module for units and
/// structures. Its module data holds a list of condition states, each
/// naming a model, animations, particle systems attached to bones and other
/// per-state options. The module switches to the state the drawable's
/// model condition flags select, and builds a new render object only when
/// that state names a different model (or different turret bones)
/// (W3DModelDraw::setModelState); states that share a model keep the
/// current render object. Tank, truck, supply and other draw modules derive
/// from it and add their own per-frame work.
///
/// In BFME 2 the same code serves the module registered as
/// "W3DScriptedModelDraw" and the modules built on it (see the group page).
/// BFME 2 code for this family is documented under either name; whether
/// BFME 2 keeps W3DModelDraw as a separate base class is not established.
/// This page describes the class's role only.
///
/// \par Modding
/// The shared model draw fields (condition states, animations, bones,
/// particle systems and the rest) come from
/// W3DModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse and are accepted by the
/// model-based draw modules, including W3DScriptedModelDraw,
/// W3DHordeModelDraw, W3DSailModelDraw, W3DTankDraw and W3DTruckDraw here,
/// and W3DSupplyDraw and W3DQuadrupedDraw on the w1021 page.
/// \see W3DScriptedModelDraw, W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated

/// \class W3DScriptedModelDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DScriptedModelDraw": BFME's general
///        model draw module, and the base that the horde, sail, tank,
///        truck, supply and quadruped draw modules build on.
///
/// It plays the part Zero Hour's W3DModelDraw plays (see W3DModelDraw for
/// what the model draw code does). Its constructor runs the DrawModule
/// constructor, sets up the module's interfaces and members, copies three
/// values from the module data to the drawable, and starts from the
/// drawable's transform (or the identity transform when there is none).
/// The constructors of W3DHordeModelDraw, W3DSailModelDraw, W3DTankDraw,
/// W3DTruckDraw, W3DSupplyDraw and W3DQuadrupedDraw run it first.
///
/// Ownership and lifetime are those of any draw module: the drawable owns
/// the module (one per \c Draw line that passes the level-of-detail check
/// on the w1021 page) and destroys it with itself; the module data belongs
/// to the template, is shared by every drawable of it and is not owned by
/// the module.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Its data comes from W3DModelDraw::friend_newModuleData, so a
/// W3DScriptedModelDraw block takes the shared model draw fields and
/// nothing else. It is registered in BFME 1 under the same name.
/// \see W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance, W3DModelDraw

/// \fn Module *W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DScriptedModelDraw": creates
///        the module for one drawable.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when a
/// drawable whose template lists the module is built. Like every instance
/// factory on these pages, it allocates the module with the global
/// \c operator \c new, runs the constructor with the drawable and the
/// module data, and returns the result as the Module base the factory
/// stores; an exception frame frees the block if the constructor throws.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's model draw module data (built by
///                    W3DModelDraw::friend_newModuleData), shared with
///                    every drawable of the template.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DScriptedModelDraw, W3DHordeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class W3DHordeModelDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DHordeModelDraw": a model draw
///        module with a horde-specific level-of-detail option.
///
/// BFME 2's constructor runs the W3DScriptedModelDraw constructor, clears
/// three members of its own and increments a global counter; what the
/// counter counts is not established here. It has a BFME 1 counterpart in
/// Open-BFME-1 (registered there under the same name); it is not in Zero
/// Hour. How it draws differently from W3DScriptedModelDraw is not
/// established here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Its block takes \c LodOptions, read by the parser
/// W3DModelDrawModuleData::parseLodOptions, and then every shared model
/// draw field: W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse adds its own
/// one-entry table before the shared one.
/// \see W3DHordeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Module data for W3DHordeModelDraw: the shared model draw data plus
///        the horde level-of-detail option.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData; its constructor
/// builds on the W3DModelDraw module data. Every drawable of the template
/// shares it. The field list is on W3DHordeModelDraw.

/// \fn Module *W3DHordeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DHordeModelDraw": creates the
///        module for one drawable.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DHordeModelDraw": creates the
///        module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// for each module line naming the module. Like every data factory on
/// these pages, it allocates the data with the global \c operator \c new,
/// runs the constructor (which sets every field's default) and, when the
/// reader is not null, calls INI::initFromINIMultiProc with the data
/// class's \c buildFieldParse, here
/// W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse (the horde table, then the
/// shared model draw table).
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to keep
///             the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data, as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see W3DHordeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class W3DTankDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DTankDraw": a model draw module that
///        scrolls tank treads and throws tread debris while the unit moves.
///
/// BFME 2's constructor runs the W3DScriptedModelDraw constructor (Zero
/// Hour derives the class from W3DModelDraw), clears the tread objects and
/// calls W3DTankDraw::createEmitters, which creates the left and right
/// tread debris particle systems named in the module data.
///
/// Zero Hour: each draw, when the unit pivots (turns while moving slower
/// than \c TreadPivotSpeedFraction of its current locomotor speed) or
/// drives at or above \c TreadDriveSpeedFraction of it, the module scrolls
/// the tread textures by \c TreadAnimationRate, a fixed step not scaled by
/// velocity. It runs the debris emitters while the unit moves on the
/// ground, with their particle speed and burst count growing with the
/// unit's speed. BFME 2's W3DTankDraw::doDrawModule follows that structure
/// but differs in detail: for example, it drops Zero Hour's motive-force
/// test (PhysicsBehavior::isMotive) before the drive scroll, and takes the
/// speed and turning state from different sources. When the model is
/// replaced, W3DTankDraw::onRenderObjRecreated rebuilds the tread objects
/// for the new render object.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of the module data, after the shared model draw fields:
/// \c TreadDebrisLeft and \c TreadDebrisRight (particle system names; the
/// constructor defaults are \c TrackDebrisDirtLeft and
/// \c TrackDebrisDirtRight), \c TreadAnimationRate (a velocity),
/// \c TreadPivotSpeedFraction and \c TreadDriveSpeedFraction (reals). The
/// names and defaults are the same as Zero Hour's.
/// \see W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleData, W3DTruckDraw

/// \fn Module *W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DTankDraw": creates the module
///        for one drawable.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance; the
/// class page describes what the constructor sets up.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared tank draw module data.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DTankDraw": creates the tank draw
///        module data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData. The
/// data object is the tank draw module data (its constructor builds on the
/// W3DModelDraw module data and sets the tread defaults), and the field
/// source, W3DTankDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse, adds the shared model
/// draw table and then the five tread fields.
///
/// \note As in Zero Hour, whose module macro declares
///       \c friend_newModuleData on the module class, this factory is
///       spelled on W3DTankDraw. The factories for the horde, sail, wake,
///       stream and streak modules are spelled on their data classes
///       instead. Retail has no symbols for either, and the registration
///       that pairs this factory with "W3DTankDraw" is its identity.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class W3DTruckDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DTruckDraw": a model draw module that
///        turns a vehicle's wheels, cab and trailer and drives its dust,
///        dirt and powerslide effects.
///
/// BFME 2's constructor runs the W3DScriptedModelDraw constructor (Zero
/// Hour derives the class from W3DModelDraw) and sets up the effect
/// handles, the cached bone indices and two members of one event class
/// (Zero Hour has two audio events here, the powerslide and landing sounds;
/// the BFME 2 class is not confirmed). Zero Hour: each frame the module spins
/// the tire bones as the vehicle moves, swings the cab and trailer bones as
/// it turns, and starts or stops the dust, dirt and powerslide particle
/// systems; it finds the bones by name in the current render object and
/// caches their indices.
/// W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated drops those cached indices when the
/// model is replaced, and W3DTruckDraw::setHidden, as in Zero Hour, runs
/// the base W3DModelDraw::setHidden and switches the emitters off when the
/// drawable is hidden.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of the module data, after the shared model draw fields:
/// - \c Dust, \c DirtSpray and \c PowerslideSpray (particle system names);
/// - tire bone names: \c LeftFrontTireBone, \c RightFrontTireBone,
///   \c LeftRearTireBone, \c RightRearTireBone, \c MidLeftFrontTireBone,
///   \c MidRightFrontTireBone, \c MidLeftRearTireBone,
///   \c MidRightRearTireBone, \c MidLeftMidTireBone and
///   \c MidRightMidTireBone, as in Zero Hour, and six more that Zero Hour
///   lacks: \c LeftFrontTireBone2, \c RightFrontTireBone2,
///   \c LeftRearTireBone2, \c RightRearTireBone2, \c MidLeftMidTireBone2
///   and \c MidRightMidTireBone2;
/// - \c TireRotationMultiplier and \c PowerslideRotationAddition (reals);
/// - \c CabBone and \c TrailerBone (bone names) with
///   \c CabRotationMultiplier, \c TrailerRotationMultiplier and
///   \c RotationDamping (reals).
///
/// The list was read from the retail executable's field table, which
/// W3DTruckDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse adds after the shared model draw
/// table.
/// \see W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleData,
///      W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated, W3DTankDraw

/// \fn Module *W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DTruckDraw": creates the module
///        for one drawable.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance; the
/// class page describes what the constructor sets up.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared truck draw module data.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DTruckDraw": creates the truck draw
///        module data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData. The
/// data object is the truck draw module data (its constructor builds on the
/// W3DModelDraw module data and sets the truck defaults), and the field
/// source, W3DTruckDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse, adds the shared model
/// draw table and then the truck fields listed on W3DTruckDraw.
///
/// \note As with W3DTankDraw::friend_newModuleData, this factory is
///       spelled on the module class, following Zero Hour's module macro;
///       its identity is the registration that pairs it with
///       "W3DTruckDraw".
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see W3DTruckDraw::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn void W3DTruckDraw::onRenderObjRecreated(void)
/// \brief Called after the model draw code replaces the truck's render
///        object: forgets the cached bones and finds them again in the new
///        model.
///
/// The truck caches the index of each bone it animates, and the previous
/// render object it found them in. Those indices belong to one render
/// object, so when the model changes they must be looked up again.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// Read from the BFME 2 body: it clears the remembered previous render
/// object and the sixteen cached tire bone indices, then calls
/// W3DTruckDraw::updateBones, which looks each bone up in the current
/// render object by the name in the module data and fills the indices
/// again.
///
/// \par Identity and donor
/// The name is not in the retail executable. The function is identified by
/// its slot in W3DTruckDraw's virtual table, compared with W3DModelDraw's,
/// and by its body, which has Zero Hour's shape. In Zero Hour the slot is
/// W3DModelDraw::onRenderObjRecreated, empty in the base class, and
/// W3DModelDraw::setModelState calls it after it builds a new render
/// object for a new model condition state. The BFME 2 caller is not
/// established here (tools/callers_of.py shows the current state); that
/// the BFME 2 model draw code calls it the same way is carried from Zero
/// Hour.
///
/// \note Zero Hour's version clears ten tire bone indices; BFME 2 clears
/// sixteen. W3DTruckDraw::updateBones fills those sixteen from the sixteen
/// tire bone fields (Zero Hour's ten plus the six ending in \c 2), and
/// keeps the cab and trailer bone indices separately. Neither version
/// clears those two here.
///
/// \see W3DTruckDraw, W3DTruckDraw::updateBones


/// \class W3DSailModelDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DSailModelDraw": a model draw module
///        that turns its model about the vertical axis toward a fixed wind
///        direction.
///
/// BFME 2's constructor runs the W3DScriptedModelDraw constructor and
/// clears the last applied angle and the flag that says one is held. The
/// module is in neither Zero Hour nor BFME 1 (whose W3DModuleFactory::init
/// does not register it).
///
/// The class overrides the last hook of W3DScriptedModelDraw's virtual
/// table, which receives the transform being prepared for drawing the
/// model. The override turns that transform about its vertical (Z) axis
/// toward a fixed direction in world space, halfway between the world X
/// and Y axes, which plays the part of the wind: it measures the angle
/// between the model's X axis and that direction, caps it at
/// \c MaxRotationDegrees (mirrored to the other side when the direction
/// lies on the model's negative Y side), and, once a previous angle is
/// held, lets the angle change by at most \c AboutDamping per call. What
/// \c BlowingThresholdDegrees does is not established; the override does
/// not read it. The hook is called from the model draw code's transform
/// adjustment (Zero Hour: W3DModelDraw::adjustTransformMtx, which BFME
/// extends), on the path where the module data names a bone to attach the
/// model to and the drawable supplies that bone's transform. That
/// adjustment runs each time W3DModelDraw::doDrawModule places the model's
/// render object, and its callers also include
/// W3DModelDraw::reactToTransformChange, W3DScriptedModelDraw::getPolygon
/// and W3DScriptedModelDraw::getRamp, so on that path the hook runs on
/// those calls too.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of the module data, after the shared model draw fields:
/// - \c MaxRotationDegrees and \c BlowingThresholdDegrees: angles, written
///   in degrees; BFME 2's INI::parseAngleReal stores them in radians.
/// - \c AboutDamping: a plain real, compared directly with the angle in
///   radians, so it is written in radians per call.
///
/// The constructor sets \c MaxRotationDegrees to zero,
/// \c BlowingThresholdDegrees to 0.25 and \c AboutDamping to 0.05; the two
/// non-zero values are stored as they are, in radians (about 14 and 3
/// degrees). With the default cap of zero the model does not turn, so a
/// block must set \c MaxRotationDegrees for the sail to follow the wind.
/// The wind direction itself is hard-coded in the override, not read from
/// INI or map data.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// The damping limit applies per call of the transform adjustment, which
/// happens at least once per draw of the model, so where it limits the
/// swing, the sail turns toward the wind faster at a higher draw rate, and
/// faster still when transform changes or polygon and ramp queries add
/// calls.
/// \see W3DSailModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DSailModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class W3DSailModelDrawModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Module data for W3DSailModelDraw: the shared model draw data plus
///        three sail settings.
///
/// Built by W3DSailModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData; its
/// constructor builds on the W3DModelDraw module data. The field list is
/// on W3DSailModelDraw.

/// \fn Module *W3DSailModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DSailModelDraw": creates the
