/// \class W3DBoatWakeModelDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DBoatWakeModelDraw": draws a wake
///        model with a moving object, scaled by how fast it goes.
///
/// It is not a model draw module: its constructor runs the DrawModule
/// constructor and clears a flag, two pointers (the wake's render object,
/// which W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::doDrawModule moves and the destructor
/// releases, and a host object the destructor unregisters the module from;
/// the host's class is not established) and the speed ratio.
/// The module is in neither Zero Hour nor BFME 1.
///
/// W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::doDrawModule keeps a speed ratio that moves toward
/// the object's locomotor's current speed divided by its maximum speed, by
/// at most a small fixed step per call. It places the wake model at the
/// drawable's position, turned to the drawable's heading, moved by the
/// configured offset and scaled by the ratio, so the wake grows as the
/// object speeds up and shrinks as it slows. W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::xfer
/// saves the DrawModule base state, the module's own version number and
/// the speed ratio; the ratio is read only from version 2 of that format,
/// so an older save leaves it at its constructor value of zero.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData: \c ModelName (text, the
/// wake model) and \c Offset (a 3D coordinate). These are its only fields;
/// the shared model draw fields do not apply.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// The speed ratio moves by a fixed step each time the module draws, so the
/// wake grows and shrinks faster at a higher draw rate.
/// \see W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Module data for W3DBoatWakeModelDraw: a wake model name and an
///        offset.
///
/// Built by W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData from its
/// own single table, W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse. The
/// field list is on W3DBoatWakeModelDraw.

/// \fn Module *W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DBoatWakeModelDraw": creates
///        the module for one drawable.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DBoatWakeModelDraw": creates the
///        module data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData, with
/// W3DBoatWakeModelDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse, a single table, as the
/// field source.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see W3DBoatWakeModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class W3DProjectileStreamDraw
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Draw module registered as "W3DProjectileStreamDraw": draws a
///        textured line through a stream of projectiles.
///
/// A Zero Hour class; its constructor runs the DrawModule constructor.
/// Zero Hour: the module reads the projectile positions recorded by the
/// \c ProjectileStreamUpdate module on the same object (the stream object,
/// which the firing weapon notifies of each projectile) and draws
/// segmented, scrolling lines through them, starting a new line where the
/// stream has a gap. \c MaxSegments, when not zero, limits the lines to
/// that many of the newest positions. BFME 2's
/// W3DProjectileStreamDraw::doDrawModule keeps Zero Hour's structure on
/// BFME 2's object layout, and W3DProjectileStreamDraw::setFullyObscuredByShroud
/// and W3DProjectileStreamDraw::xfer are also present. BFME 1 does not
/// register the module.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData: \c Texture (text),
/// \c Width, \c TileFactor and \c ScrollRate (reals) and \c MaxSegments
/// (whole number), the same names as Zero Hour's. Zero Hour: the same
/// object also needs a \c ProjectileStreamUpdate module, from which the
/// draw module takes the projectile positions, and a weapon creates that
/// stream object from the object template named by its
/// \c ProjectileStreamName field.
/// \see W3DProjectileStreamDraw::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Module data for W3DProjectileStreamDraw: texture, width, tiling,
///        scroll rate and segment limit of the stream's lines.
///
/// Built by W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData from
/// its own single table. The field list is on W3DProjectileStreamDraw.

/// \fn Module *W3DProjectileStreamDraw::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "W3DProjectileStreamDraw":
///        creates the module for one drawable.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DScriptedModelDraw::friend_newModuleInstance.
///
/// \param thing       The drawable being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared
///                    W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DProjectileStreamDraw": creates the
///        module data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData, with
/// W3DProjectileStreamDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse, a single table, as
/// the field source.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see W3DProjectileStreamDraw::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class W3DStreakDrawModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_w3d_draw_module_factories_more
/// \brief Module data for the draw module registered as "W3DStreakDraw":
///        length, width, colour, texture and segment count of a streak.
///
/// W3DStreakDraw is a BFME 1 class (Open-BFME-1 has its constructor,
/// destructor and data), not a Zero Hour one. Built once per module line
/// by W3DStreakDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData from its own single
/// table and shared by every drawable of the template. What the streak
/// module draws is not described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields: \c Length and \c Width (reals), \c Additive (yes/no),
/// \c Color (an RGB colour), \c Texture (text), \c NumSegments (whole
/// number) and \c WeatherTexture, which has a parser of its own. The list
/// was read from the retail executable's field table.
/// \see W3DStreakDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *W3DStreakDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "W3DStreakDraw": creates the module
///        data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as W3DHordeModelDrawModuleData::friend_newModuleData, with
/// W3DStreakDrawModuleData::buildFieldParse, a single table, as the field
/// source. W3DModuleFactory::init pairs it with W3DStreakDraw's instance
/// factory, which is not covered here.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see W3DStreakDrawModuleData
